---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Services — Pravine Mani · AI, SEO, Marketing Automation & Agentic OS Consultancy" description="Toronto consultancy. Four focus areas: AI workflows, programmatic SEO + GEO, marketing automation, Agentic OS. Engagement shapes scoped to fit. Free 30-min call.">


<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><span class="gr">$</span> cd ~/services <span class="you">→ what i build for you</span></div>
  <h1>Four engagement shapes.<br><span class="accent">Founding pricing on Audit + Sprint.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">Four focus areas — <a href="/services/ai/">AI</a>, <a href="/services/seo/">SEO + GEO</a>, <a href="/services/marketing-automation/">marketing automation</a>, and <a href="/services/agentic-os/">Agentic OS</a> — built across four engagement shapes: a <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Free Workflow Teardown</strong> top-of-funnel, plus Audit / Sprint / Custom. <strong style="color: var(--green);">Founding rates live on Audit + Sprint — 3 slots each, reverts to standard after.</strong></p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a href="/contact/" class="cta-btn">Book a 30-min call →</a>
    <a href="#builds" class="cta-btn secondary">See sample builds</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Mid-page CTA band -->
<div class="cta-band">
  <div class="cta-band-inner">
    <div class="left">
      <span class="lab">AVAILABILITY</span>
      <span class="h"><span class="acc">Currently taking new engagements</span> · scoping calls open</span>
    </div>
    <a href="/contact/" class="cta-btn">Check fit →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Canadian grant callout -->
<div class="grant-callout reveal">
  <div class="grant-inner">
    <span class="grant-flag">CA · GRANT</span>
    <div class="grant-body">
      <span class="grant-h">Canadian small business?</span>
      <span class="grant-sub">Up to <strong>$15K of an engagement</strong> can be grant-covered through federal programs like <strong>CDAP</strong> (Canada Digital Adoption Program) and <strong>IRAP</strong> (NRC Industrial Research Assistance). I scope inside those grant frameworks regularly.</span>
    </div>
    <a href="/contact/" class="grant-cta">Talk grant fit →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== PRIMARY ENGAGEMENTS ===== -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">engagement shapes</div>
    <h2>Four shapes. One operator. Every project fits.</h2>
    <p>Each shape is productized — fixed scope, fixed deliverables, written quote. <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Free Teardown</strong> is the no-friction entry (30 min, $0). <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Audit</strong> for "we're not sure where AI fits yet" (founding: $1,500). <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Sprint</strong> when the workflow is one-line-able (founding: $2,500). <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Custom</strong> for anything multi-workflow (from $12K).</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 00 · FREE WORKFLOW TEARDOWN -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="teardown">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1" style="color: #ffd84a;"><span class="pulse" style="background: #ffd84a;"></span>00 · FREE WORKFLOW TEARDOWN</div>
        <h3>Send me one workflow you hate doing. I'll map the automation.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time" style="color: #ffd84a;">FREE · 30 MIN</div>
        <div class="slots">5 SLOTS / MO</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT YOU GET</h4>
        <p>A 30-min live call (or async — send a Loom + brief). I map one workflow end-to-end, identify the 2–3 highest-leverage automation moves, and hand you a verbal ROI estimate + a recommended next step.</p>
        <p><strong>No deck.</strong> No deliverable PDF. No pitch. Just operator-to-operator signal on what to fix first.</p>
        <p><strong>Right starting point</strong> for: founders unsure where AI fits, teams already paying for tools that don't talk to each other, or anyone with a workflow that's eating their week.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT WE DO ON THE CALL</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>You walk me through one workflow (5 min)</li>
          <li>I ask 4–5 sharp questions to find the leak</li>
          <li>I map the automation live, on screen</li>
          <li>Verbal ROI: hours/month + dollar estimate</li>
          <li>One specific recommended next step</li>
          <li>If it makes sense, we scope a Sprint right there</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta" style="color: #ffd84a;"><strong>$0 · 5 SLOTS / MONTH</strong> · NO OBLIGATION</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ BOOK TEARDOWN</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 01 · AUDIT -->
  <div class="tier-card featured reveal" id="audit">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1"><span class="pulse"></span>01 · AI SYSTEM AUDIT</div>
        <h3>Find where AI, SEO, or automation gives you back the most hours.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time">FIXED-SCOPE WEEK · MOST POPULAR</div>
        <div class="slots">LIMITED CAPACITY</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT YOU GET</h4>
        <p>A focused week of operator-to-operator analysis. I interview you, watch how your week actually goes, map your workflows, and find the 3–5 places AI gives you back real, measurable time.</p>
        <p>You leave with: a prioritized opportunity list, vendor recommendations, monthly cost projections, and a concrete 30-day build plan you (or I) can execute against.</p>
        <p><strong>Right starting point</strong> if you're not sure where to point AI yet, or you've tried tools and nothing stuck.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>DELIVERABLES</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>3× founder interviews · 60 min each</li>
          <li>Current-state workflow map</li>
          <li>Ranked opportunity list · effort × impact</li>
          <li>Vendor + cost projections per opportunity</li>
          <li>30-day execution plan with milestones</li>
          <li>60-min handoff call + Loom walkthrough</li>
          <li>Option to roll into a build sprint</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta"><strong style="color: var(--green);">FOUNDING 3: $1,500</strong> · 3 SLOTS OPEN · REMOTE</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ BOOK AUDIT CALL</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 02 · SPRINT -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="sprint">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1" style="color: var(--red);"><span class="pulse" style="background: var(--red);"></span>02 · 48-HOUR BUILD SPRINT</div>
        <h3>Ship the one workflow that's been on your list for months.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time" style="color: var(--red);">FIXED-SCOPE BUILD</div>
        <div class="slots">LIMITED CAPACITY</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT YOU GET</h4>
        <p>Productized scope, fixed timeline. We agree on one specific workflow Monday morning, I deliver it deployed + documented by Wednesday EOD.</p>
        <p>If the workflow isn't "send this draft to my inbox at 6am" specific, the sprint doesn't fit — that's deliberate. The 48-hour clock forces clarity on both sides.</p>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> daily morning brief, weekly metrics report, sales follow-up automation, content cross-poster, AI-graded inbox triage, etc.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>DELIVERABLES</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>One workflow · clear input + output</li>
          <li>Deployed on your Vercel (or mine)</li>
          <li>README · cost projection · env-var spec</li>
          <li>15-min handoff Loom + architecture diagram</li>
          <li>14 days of post-sprint bug fixes</li>
          <li>You own the code outright</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta"><strong style="color: var(--green);">FOUNDING 3: $2,500</strong> · 3 SLOTS OPEN · 50% UPFRONT</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ BOOK SPRINT CALL</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 03 · CUSTOM -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="custom">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1" style="color: var(--blue);"><span class="pulse" style="background: var(--blue);"></span>03 · CUSTOM BUILD</div>
        <h3>When the project is too big for a sprint, too specific for an agency.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time" style="color: var(--blue);">QUOTE-BASED</div>
        <div class="slots">LIMITED CAPACITY</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT YOU GET</h4>
        <p>For multi-workflow builds that need more than a sprint. We do a free 30-min scoping call. I send you a written spec + quote within 24 hrs. Once you sign, I work to milestones with daily updates and a demo at each milestone.</p>
        <p><strong>Examples I've shipped:</strong> end-to-end content engine (RSS → 6 platform variants), Whop-integrated onboarding system, competitor watch with weekly digest, AI-graded inbox triage, custom community workspace.</p>
        <p>If your idea isn't on the list below — that's what this tier is for. Custom is the default when scope doesn't fit a productized box.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>DELIVERABLES</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>30-min scoping call (free)</li>
          <li>Written spec within 24 hrs</li>
          <li>Milestone-based delivery</li>
          <li>Your stack OR my recommended stack</li>
          <li>Daily progress updates</li>
          <li>Architecture diagram + cost projections</li>
          <li>Full source + deployment instructions</li>
          <li>30 days of post-launch fixes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta">FROM $12K · MILESTONE-PAID</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ START SCOPING</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== WHO I'M NOT FOR (filter block) ===== -->
<section class="section" id="not-for">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label" style="color: var(--red);">honest filter</div>
    <h2>Who I'm <em>not</em> for.</h2>
    <p>Saves both of us the call. If any of these are you, the engagement won't work — and I'd rather say so up front than waste your time.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="not-for-grid">
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>Enterprises with procurement cycles</h4>
      <p>You need a vendor MSA, a 6-week security review, and a SOC 2 audit before signing. I'm one person — that overhead breaks the economics. Hire a real agency.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>n8n / Make / Zapier rebuilds only</h4>
      <p>If you want a no-code workflow strung together in a visual editor, I'm the wrong consultant. I work in code. If your stack is correct as-is, I'll say so and refund.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>Sub-$2K projects</h4>
      <p>Below mid four-figures, the scoping overhead is bigger than the work. Use the <a href="#probe">Workflow Probe</a> ($200-500) for one-off advice — or hire a freelance dev.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>Hourly billing engagements</h4>
      <p>Every engagement is fixed-scope, fixed-price. Hourly aligns nobody's incentives. If you need T&amp;M billing, we won't be able to work together.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>AI-safety / AGI / RLHF research</h4>
      <p>Not my lane. Hire someone closer to the frontier labs. I build ops workflows, not alignment models.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>Customer-service chatbot work</h4>
      <p>Saturated category. Intercom Fin, Forethought, Ada exist and are better at it than I'll ever be. I'll send you to them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="not-for-foot">
    <p>If you're still here after that filter — <a href="/contact/">book a 30-min call</a>. Quick fit-check, free, ends with a written quote within 24 hours.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SPECIFIC BUILDS GRID ===== -->
<section class="section" id="builds">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">sample builds</div>
    <h2>Ten things I've actually built — sprintable, customizable, or skippable.</h2>
    <p>These are the actual workflows I've built for myself or clients. Each can ship as a 48-hour sprint OR be customized to your stack. <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">If your need isn't here, that's a Custom Build engagement.</strong> Scoping is free either way.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="builds-grid">

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">$</div><span class="num">BUILD 01</span></div>
      <h4>Content Engine</h4>
      <p>One source article → 6+ platform-specific variants (X thread, LinkedIn carousel, newsletter, native video script, Reddit, podcast intro). RSS-triggered. AI-drafted, you approve before ship.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.04/run</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">▸</div><span class="num">BUILD 02</span></div>
      <h4>Customer Onboarding Sequence</h4>
      <p>Whop webhook (or Stripe/Lemon Squeezy) → Claude personalizes welcome → tags subscriber → triggers Day-0 to Day-30 sequence. Used on AIOpsForge.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.012/signup</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">▣</div><span class="num">BUILD 03</span></div>
      <h4>Daily Operations Brief</h4>
      <p>06:00 ET morning summary in your inbox: stalled deals, urgent items, today's priorities, metrics movement. Pulls from CRM + calendar + email. AI flags what matters.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.08/day</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">◐</div><span class="num">BUILD 04</span></div>
      <h4>Competitor Watch + Weekly Intel</h4>
      <p>Scans 6+ competitors across pricing pages, launch blogs, X, changelogs. Flags pricing changes + launches. Weekly intel report drafted Sunday night for Monday read.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.12/day</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">⌘</div><span class="num">BUILD 05</span></div>
      <h4>Claude Code Stack Setup</h4>
      <p>Install + configure Claude Code for your whole team. Custom CLAUDE.md, sub-agents, hooks, MCP servers tuned to your stack. Includes training + cheatsheet.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>1-DAY ENGAGEMENT</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">⊞</div><span class="num">BUILD 06</span></div>
      <h4>Design System Application</h4>
      <p>Apply a unified design language to your existing app. Token system, component patterns, voice rules. Includes audit + migration plan. Built on Terminal DS or your brand.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>1–2 WEEKS</span><span class="ev">CUSTOM</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">◊</div><span class="num">BUILD 07</span></div>
      <h4>Community Platform Build</h4>
      <p>Full community workspace — Whop / Skool / custom on your stack. Member auth, gated content, weekly drop cadence, AI coach, automated onboarding. Reference: AIOpsForge.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>3–4 WEEKS</span><span class="ev">CUSTOM</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">⌖</div><span class="num">BUILD 08</span></div>
      <h4>SEO + GEO Infrastructure</h4>
      <p>Schema markup, JSON-LD, OG images per page, sitemap, robots, FAQ schema, llms.txt for AI-search engines. Built for ranking in Google + Perplexity + ChatGPT-Search.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>3–5 DAYS</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">∞</div><span class="num">BUILD 09</span></div>
      <h4>Lead-Magnet → CRM Pipeline</h4>
      <p>Landing page + gated PDF → Beehiiv/Kit/ConvertKit → tagged + sequenced. AI personalizes follow-ups. Stripe/Whop checkout wired in. Plausible analytics + funnel tracking.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>3–5 DAYS</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">⚙</div><span class="num">BUILD 10</span></div>
      <h4>MCP Server (Custom)</h4>
      <p>Build a custom Model Context Protocol server that connects Claude to your internal tools, data, or APIs. Example: Notion-MCP, Linear-MCP, your-CRM-MCP.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>2–4 DAYS</span><span class="ev">CUSTOM</span></div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="dont-do reveal">
    <div class="lab">— SO WE DON'T WASTE EACH OTHER'S TIME —</div>
    <h3>What I don't build.</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Chatbots for customer support (wrong fit)</li>
      <li>Anything in trading / crypto / gambling</li>
      <li>AGI / AI safety research</li>
      <li>Equity-only engagements</li>
      <li>Mobile apps (iOS / Android native)</li>
      <li>3D / animation / video editing</li>
      <li>Anything requiring ongoing 1:1 support &gt;10 hr/wk</li>
      <li>"Disrupt the legal industry" plays</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== PROCESS ===== -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">how the engagement goes</div>
    <h2>Four steps from "interesting" to shipped.</h2>
    <p>Lean, async-defaulted, written-first. No "discovery deck," no 60-min kickoff calls just to align timezones.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--border); border: 1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom: 24px;">
    <div style="background: var(--bg-card); padding: 24px 22px;">
      <div style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--green); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px;">STEP 01</div>
      <h4 style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 6px;">DM the form.</h4>
      <p style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55;">4 questions, ~5 min: what's broken, who you are, when you need it, ballpark expectation. I read everything personally.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background: var(--bg-card); padding: 24px 22px;">
      <div style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--green); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px;">STEP 02</div>
      <h4 style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 6px;">Free 30-min call.</h4>
      <p style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55;">Within 48 hrs. Confirm fit, sharpen scope, agree on which engagement matches. No pitch deck.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background: var(--bg-card); padding: 24px 22px;">
      <div style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--green); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px;">STEP 03</div>
      <h4 style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 6px;">Written quote.</h4>
      <p style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55;">Within 24 hrs of the call. Fixed price, payment terms, milestones, mutual NDA. Sign with a Stripe link.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background: var(--bg-card); padding: 24px 22px;">
      <div style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--green); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px;">STEP 04</div>
      <h4 style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 6px;">I ship · you review.</h4>
      <p style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55;">Daily progress notes. Demo on milestone. Final handover with README, deployment, Loom walkthrough.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Mid-page CTA #2 -->
<div class="cta-band">
  <div class="cta-band-inner">
    <div class="left">
      <span class="lab">STILL DECIDING?</span>
      <span class="h">Book a <span class="acc">30-min scoping call</span> — zero pitch, just operator-to-operator</span>
    </div>
    <a href="/contact/" class="cta-btn">Book the call →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== FAQ ===== -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">questions</div>
    <h2>The ones I actually get.</h2>
    <p>If yours isn't here, ask on the call. Every objection below is a real one I've heard.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-block">
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What do prices actually look like?</summary><p><span class="acc">Founding rates on the cards above are real and time-limited.</span> Audit at $1,500 and Sprint at $2,500 are locked in for the first 3 of each — when they fill, standard rates resume. Custom builds start at $12K and quote inside 24 hours of the call. The 30-min teardown call is always free.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What stack do you build on?</summary><p><span class="acc">Claude Code + Vercel (serverless + cron + KV) + Anthropic API.</span> I work in your stack if it matches — TypeScript, Next.js, Supabase, Stripe, Beehiiv, Whop are all comfortable. I <strong>won't</strong> build on n8n, Make, or Zapier — fragile, expensive at scale, and you can't read the code six months from now.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Who owns the code?</summary><p><span class="acc">You do, outright.</span> All deliverables are work-for-hire under a written agreement. You get full source, the deployment, and the right to modify or sell. I keep no claim.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Why fixed price instead of hourly?</summary><p>Hourly aligns incentives badly — I'd be incentivized to take longer, you'd be incentivized to micro-manage. Fixed-price aligns us on outcome: we both want the thing done well, fast, and right the first time.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What if I'm in a different timezone?</summary><p>I'm in Toronto (ET). Async-default works for most engagements — Slack/email + recorded Loom updates. Live calls in your timezone within 9am–9pm ET; outside that, written-first.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What if the scope changes mid-project?</summary><p>For sprints: scope is fixed, period. For audits + custom builds: anything outside the written spec is a separate quote. I'll tell you the impact before you decide, never silently re-scope.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Can you start next week?</summary><p>Usually yes for sprints, sometimes for custom builds. Audits typically book 2–3 weeks out. Always ask — calendars change.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What if I'm not sure I need an AI engagement at all?</summary><p>Book the call anyway. If I don't think AI is the right fix, <span class="acc">I'll tell you that on the call</span> and point you to who or what is. The 30 minutes are free; the honest answer is the deliverable.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

